{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Good Leadership"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The GROW Model"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le06ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "coach "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who trains a person or team"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At each stage, the coach will ask relevant open questions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about the GROW model. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "coachee"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who receives training from a coach"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The coach's questions are designed to help the coachee establish an appropriate objective."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "coaching"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the activity of \u200bproviding \u200btraining for \u200bpeople or helping to prepare them for something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This stage of the coaching conversation is all about helping the coachee understand their present situation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "context"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bsituation within which something \u200b\u200bhappens, and that can \u200bhelp \u200bexplain it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:They should think about their objective in the context of the real world. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "action point"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a specific for action to be taken, typically one arising from a meeting"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The final stage of the this model is for the coach to ask the coachee questions that will help them identify some action points. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "put something into practice "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "start to use it and see if it is effective"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  It is important to establish their willingness to put these actions into practice and move towards their goal."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Purpose Clauses including To-Infinitives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " The most common way for you to express purpose is to use a to-infinitive (called an infinitive of purpose)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use to-infinitive (within a reason clause) especially when you want to express one particular purpose."}, {"type": "text", "content": " For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I called <span class=\"strong\">to find out if she was still there</span>. <br/> Ben has gone into the city <span class=\"strong\">to do some research</span>. <br/> <span class=\"strong\">To get a good seat</span>, you need to book ahead. <br/> I'm writing <span class=\"strong\">to enquire about the availability of your staff</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "At this stage, the coach's questions are designed to help the coachee establish an appropriate objective."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This stage of the coaching conversation is all about helping the coachee to understand their present situation and to think about their objective in the context of the real world. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The GROW model provides a simple but effective framework for coaches to help coachees establish an objective, achieve a deeper understanding of the situation they face, "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Expressing Intention and Willingness: <span class=\"italic\">Will </span>and <span class=\"italic\">Would</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to express intention to do something or a willingness to do something, you can use the verbs <span class=\"italic\">will </span>and <span class=\"italic\">would.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Context is particularly important to understand the exact meaning of each verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Mary <span class=\"strong\">will </span>translate for you - she speaks French.</span> (willingness) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">ll</span> do it - I don't mind. </span>(willingness) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">won't </span>be coming later. </span>(intention) <br/><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">Would </span>you mind helping me, please? </span>(willingness) <br/><span class=\"italic\"> I'<span class=\"strong\">ll </span>call you later. </span>(intention)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the examples from the text. Keep the context in mind as you do."}, {"type": "example", "content": "At each stage, the coach will ask relevant open questions. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "These questions will encourage the coachee to reflect deeply."}, {"type": "example", "content": "How do you feel this process will help you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The coach will help the coachee explore the options that are available to them. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The final stage of the this model is for the coach to ask the coachee questions that will help them identify some action points."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Work with a partner. One person is the coach and the other the coachee."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do the GROW model process and put your ideas on a poster."}, {"type": "text", "content": "GOAL: Decide on a goal. Goals need to be SMART (specific, measurable, acceptable, realistic, timely)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "REALITY: Self-evaluate and identify the obstacles in your path."}, {"type": "text", "content": "OPTIONS: Brainstorm ideas that can help solve your problems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "WILL: Establish what is necessary to achieve your goals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch roles with your partner"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Next, present your posters to the class."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brainstorm ideas with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I self-evaluate."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create goals that are SMART."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I establish options and acknowledge the necessary steps needed to achieve these goals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I facilitate my partner as they work through a GROW model."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my GROW model ideas to the class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express willingness or intention to do 