eedback": "Correct!"}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 11}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn11le06ob10re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "Within the GROW model there are four key areas which the coach and coachee should explore. At each stage, the coach will ask relevant open questions. These questions will encourage the coachee to reflect deeply, achieve a better understanding of the situation in question, and start to identify some potential solutions.</br></br>Stage one - Goal:\nAt this stage, the coach's questions are designed to help the coachee establish an appropriate objective. The coach might ask some or all of the following questions: What do you want to achieve? How do you feel this process will help you? What do you think it will take for this process to be a success?", "id": 1, "image": "engenn11le06ob10re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "35400", "text": "Stage two - Reality:\nThis stage of the coaching conversation is all about helping the coachee to understand their present situation and to think about their objective in the context of the real world. Questions from the coach might include: What challenges or obstacles do expect to encounter? How will you overcome them?</br></br>Stage three - Options:\nThe coach will help the coachee explore the options that are available to them. Questions might include: What options are available to you? What are the pros and cons of each option?", "id": 2, "image": "engenn11le06ob10re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "65450", "text": "Stage four - Will/Way forward:\nThe final stage of the this model is for the coach to ask the coachee questions that will help them identify some action points and establish their willingness to put these actions into practice and move towards their goal. Questions might include: How do you intend to put your chosen options into action? What does achieving your goal mean to you?</br></br>The GROW model provides a simple but effective framework for coaches to help coachees establish an objective, achieve a deeper understanding of the situation they face, explore the options that are available to them and identify an appropriate way forward. By asking open questions at each stage of the framework, the coach will facilitate, rather than direct, the conversation and, in doing so, will enable the coachee to arrive at their own conclusions.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn11le06ob10re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le06ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le06ob10re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": [], "title": ""}], "id": 0}]}